  "landfallEstimate": "To cross south Andhra Pradesh",
  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 14\nDEMS-RSMC SPECIAL TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 03.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 14 FOR NORTH INDIAN OCEAN (THE BAY OF\nBENGAL AND ARABIAN SEA) ISSUED AT 0210 UTC OF 03.11.2026 BASED ON 0000 UTC\nOF 03.11.2026\nSub: - Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] crossed South Andhra Pradesh\nCoast\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over Westcentral Bay of Bengal close to\nSouth Andhra Pradesh Coast moved north-northwestwards with a speed of 8 kmph during past 6 hrs and\ncrossed the south Andhra Pradesh coast between Nellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh) and Narsapur (43187,\nAndhra Pradesh), near Latitude 15.53\u00b0N and Longitude 80.22\u00b0E, close to Ongole (43221, Andhra\nPradesh), about 40 km southwest of Bapatla (43220, Andhra Pradesh), 80 km north-northeast of Kavali\n(43243, Andhra Pradesh), 120 km west-southwest of Machilipatnam (43185, Andhra Pradesh) and 130 km\nnorth of Nellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh) during 2200 UTC of 2nd November to 0000 UTC of 3rd\nNovember as a Sever Cyclonic Storm with maximum sustain wind speed of 100-110 kmph gusting to 120\nkmph.\nIt is likely to continue to move North-northwestwards and weaken gradually into a cyclonic storm (wind\nspeed reaching 80-90 kmph gusting to 100 kmph) by 0600 UTC and further into a deep depression (wind\nspeed reaching 55-65 kmph gusting to 75 kmph) by 1800 UTC of 03rd November.\nIt is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather Radars at Machilipatnam and Vishakhapatnam.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak: Cloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-\n25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very Intense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of\ndepression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-66% and HIGH:67-100%\nThis is a guidance Bulletin for WMO/ESCAP Panel Member countries. Visit respective National websites for Country specific Bulletins.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n03.11.26/0000 15.6/80.2 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0600 15.9/80.1 80-90 gusting to 100 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1200 16.3/80.0 65-75 gusting to 85 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1800 16.7/80.0 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\n04.11.26/0000 17.2/80.0 25-35 gusting to 45 Well Marked Low Pressure Area\nThe estimated central pressure is 995.0 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 55 kt\ngusting to 65kt.\nNellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh) reported mean sea level (MSLP) of 1010.1 hPa, 24 hours pressure\nchange (P24) as 0.7 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed (MSW) as 2000/04kt, Kavali (43243,\nAndhra Pradesh) reported MSLP of 1009.5 hPa, P24 as -0.7 hPa and MSW 2700/05kt, Bapatla\n(43220, Andhra Pradesh) reported MSLP of 1006.8 hPa, P24 as -3.5 hPa and MSW 700/13kt,\nOngole (43221, Andhra Pradesh) reported MSLP of 999.8 hPa, P24 as -9.9 hPa and MSW\n2900/23kt.\nAs per latest INSAT 3DS imagery based on 0000 UTC, Vortex (Murasu) over West-central bay off\nAndhra Pradesh coast and neighbourhood centered near 15.5N / 80.3E. Intensity of the system is\nT",
